# wsg settings. Copy to ~/.config/wsg/config and adjust to taste.

# Where workspaces are created.
WS_ROOT="$HOME/workspaces"

# Command that `ws <slug>` uses to launch the agent. If unset, ws asks on first run
# and writes it here. claude resumes the workspace's previous session, codex gets
# --add-dir for attached directories; any other command is run as-is.
# WSG_AGENT="claude"

# Language of the interview, CLI messages and ws: en or ru. If unset, taken from the locale
# (LC_ALL, LC_MESSAGES, LANG). Workspace files are always English. ws picks up a change in a
# new terminal; setting it here is more reliable than a LANG exported later in .zshrc.
# WSG_LANG="ru"

# Tracker prefix: if you answer the ticket question with just a number,
# the link is built as "$WSG_TRACKER_URL$TICKET".
# WSG_TRACKER_URL="https://your-tracker.example.com/browse/"

# Your personal file of rules for working with the agent (how to review, what not to do without asking).
# If set, the generator offers to copy a digest of it into the workspace's AGENTS.md:
# Codex has its own file chain, and this file isn't part of it.
# WSG_GLOBAL_MEMORY="$HOME/.config/agent-rules.md"

# Context file one level above the workspaces that the agent loads in every session.
# Only counted toward the always-on budget in `wsg --check`.
# WSG_PARENT_CONTEXT="$HOME/CLAUDE.md"
